{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 5–10 days show a clear positive slope (new highs / higher lows), add an upward bias to the entire path. Heuristic: +0.5 to +1.0 €/t for days 1–5, +2 to +4 €/t for days 6–15, +6 to +12 €/t for days 16–30.",
    "Horizon error grows with time: the model’s level drifts too low beyond ~1 week. Apply a linearly increasing uplift with horizon (near-zero at day 1, ramping to ~+10–15 €/t by day 30 in strong rallies).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the forecast reacts too slowly to regime shifts (breakout from ~65–70 to ~75–83). If price breaks above the 20–30d range high, replace mean-reversion behavior with trend-following (carry forward momentum) for at least the next 10–15 days.",
    "False mean reversion: model repeatedly predicts pullbacks to ~66–71 while realized prices continue trending up. Suppress mean reversion when realized volatility is rising and closes are near the upper band; instead anchor forecasts to recent highs (e.g., last close or 5d average) plus a modest positive drift.",
    "Underestimation of volatility/upside tails: realized outcomes show larger upside moves than forecast. Widen the upside distribution / shift the central path upward in rally regimes; do not cap prices near the recent mean."
  ]
}
